      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildCSS": "- Do NOT use separate file name. Put all css in a `<style>` tag in the head of the index.html file\n- Do NOT use relative units. Use px values.\n- You should generate both HTML and CSS at the same time\n- Keep all explanations short, concise, and simple.",
        "buildHTML": "- Do not create a style.css file - put all css updates in a <style> tag in the head.\n- Do NOT use IDs or class on elements\n- Do NOT generate links or buttons\n- Generate both HTML and CSS at the same time\n- Never generate placeholder images or videos. If the user implies they want an image, generate an empty `<img src=\"\" />` tag and tell the user they need to upload images to their project.\n- If the user asks to generate images: explain that you cannot generate new images but can insert any images that the user uploads to the project\n- If the user asks to insert an image from an external URL: explain that for security reasons, you cannot use external URLs for images. Instead, suggest that the user will eventually be able to upload their own images that can be added to webpages.\n- Keep all explanations short, concise, and simple."
